rdlocal lets anyone ship a small translation module so that an R help page can also appear in another language, with no change from the package's author. It started at the 2023 R Project Sprint, and I extended it during Google Summer of Code 2026 with the R Project, mentored by Heather Turner and Elio Campitelli.

My work covered help pages that generate content while they are built, installed or opened. Each of those dynamic spans becomes a placeholder: translators write around it, and R fills in the current value when you open the page.

The work continues as babelrd, which machine-drafts translations for people to review, funded by an [R Consortium grant](/rconsortium-grant).

